1. DEFINITIONS

  "Licensor" means Alexander Fetisov (Portable Labs), the copyright owner.

  "Software" means Daxis in source or compiled form, as published by the
  Licensor, including its documentation and media.

  "You" means the individual or organisation exercising rights under this
  licence. Use by an employee, contractor or agent on behalf of an
  organisation is use by that organisation. An organisation includes its
  Affiliates.

  "Affiliate" means any entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under
  common control with an organisation, where control means more than 50% of
  the voting interests or the power to direct management.

  "Individual" means a natural person using the Software for personal,
  educational, research or hobby purposes, or for their own professional work
  as a sole trader.

  "Non-profit" means a registered charity, a not-for-profit organisation, or a
  public or not-for-profit educational or research institution.

  "Small Business" means a for-profit organisation that, together with its
  Affiliates, has fewer than 50 people (employees plus full-time-equivalent
  contractors) and less than AUD 10 million in total annual revenue, both
  measured over its most recently completed financial year.

  "Major Consultancy" means an organisation that, together with its
  Affiliates:
    (a) provides consulting, advisory, professional services, systems
        integration, managed IT services or outsourcing to third parties as a
        material part of its business; and
    (b) has 1,000 or more people, or AUD 100 million or more in total annual
        revenue.
  Examples include (without limitation) Accenture, Deloitte, PwC, EY, KPMG,
  Capgemini, IBM Consulting, Cognizant, Infosys, Tata Consultancy Services,
  Wipro and their Affiliates.

  "Other For-Profit Organisation" means any for-profit organisation that is
  neither a Small Business nor a Major Consultancy.

  "Modify" means to alter, adapt, translate, refactor, port, or create a
  derivative work of the Software or any part of it, including copying any
  part of its source code into other software.

  "Contribution" means code, documentation or other material submitted to the
  Licensor for inclusion in the official Daxis repository.


